# RR3 Switch port -- what is deliberately NOT in git.
#
# The working tree is ~57 GB. Almost all of it is either a downloaded toolchain,
# a generated data volume, or a build product. None of it can be recovered from
# a commit, and committing it would make the history unusable. Everything that
# represents actual WORK -- source, scripts, docs, the guest binary, and the
# experimental record -- is tracked.
#
# Rule of thumb used below: keep anything a person wrote; ignore anything a
# tool produced.
#
# NOTE: git does not support trailing "# comment" on a pattern line. A line
# like "dist/   # the release tree" is parsed as one long pattern that matches
# nothing, and the directory silently gets committed. Every note here is on
# its own comment line, and that is deliberate.

# --- toolchains and package caches -----------------------------------------
# .tools/ is the project-local devkitPro / libnx tree (~12 GB).
.tools/

# --- downloaded asset packs ------------------------------------------------
# Three texture-format variants of the same game, ~6.1-6.6 GB each. They are the
# source data every romfs is generated from.
*数据包*.zip
*.7z
*.7z.001
*.7z.002

# --- generated data volumes -------------------------------------------------
# Rebuilt by tools/prepare_rr3_external_data.py + build_romfs from the packs.
*.romfs
# dist/ is the release tree and holds all seven volumes (~9.7 GB).
dist/
# reference/ holds the original container images, same volumes (~9.0 GB).
reference/

# --- build products ---------------------------------------------------------
# .build/ holds intermediate objects AND the eden-runs archives (~8.4 GB).
.build/
native-switch/build/
native-switch/*.nro
native-switch/*.elf
native-switch/*.map
native-switch/*.nacp
# The embedded romfs image is a build product; its source tree IS tracked.
native-switch/rr3.romfs

# --- reverse-engineering databases ------------------------------------------
# Regenerable from reverse/native/arm64/libRealRacing3.so with Ghidra.
ghidra-scratch/
ghidra-work/
reverse/ghidra-projects/

# --- guest APK --------------------------------------------------------------
# 112 MB, user-supplied and unmodified. The guest .so extracted from it IS
# tracked, because the build links against it.
*.apk

# ===========================================================================
# Everything below is EA / Apple proprietary material. The remote
# (github.com/ArakiW/rr3-switch) is PUBLIC and already carries only the
# port's own source, so this boundary must not be crossed.
# ===========================================================================
# The guest binary itself (33 MB, two working copies). The build needs it, so
# it stays on disk and is simply never committed.
native-switch/romfs/libRealRacing3.so
reverse/native/
# Decompiled Java from the guest APK (24,649 files). EA's source.
reverse/java/
# EA assets pulled back out of the depot textures/atlases.
analysis/rr3-ui-source/
# Third-party font pack, 0.33 GB, fetched not authored.
AlibabaPuHuiTi-3/
# Decoded texture dumps.
*.pvr
*.dds
# native-switch/romfs/ holds the game's own text (text_en.txt / text_cn-Hans.txt,
# ~5.8 MB of EA localisation), FMOD's libfmodex.so, and the Noto CJK font. The
# remote already carries source only, so this stays out for the same reason.
native-switch/romfs/
# Vendored third-party runtime, pulled from the guest package rather than
# authored here.
native-switch/libNimble.so
native-switch/libfmodex.so
native-switch/libc++_shared.so

# --- unrelated third-party material -----------------------------------------
# analysis/gta5-docx-struct/ and analysis/gta5-switch-bundle-report.json are a
# 72-word Chinese how-to plus its screenshots for installing a pirated GTA V NSP,
# and a file-level manifest of that pirated bundle (103 files / 103 GB, NCA
# container offsets, a local E:\QLDownload crack-release path). Neither belongs
# to this port and neither belongs on a public remote. skills/
# source-recompile-porting/references/gta5-switch-case-study.md is the
# self-limiting writeup that cites this evidence; it stays, these do not.
analysis/gta5-docx-struct/
analysis/gta5-switch-bundle-report.json

# --- Python bytecode ---------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerated on every test run. All 11 tests are source-tracked; the .pyc files
# were the only reason __pycache__ showed up in the snapshot.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- scratch -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the reverse-engineering sub-agents park throwaway scripts. They are
# numbered and disposable; the real analysis tooling is tracked under
# tools/guest-analysis/ and must not be confused with this directory.
native-switch/guest-analysis/scratch/
guest-analysis/scratch/
# .local/ holds one-shot repair and probe scripts written during an
# investigation. Durable checks live in tools/ instead -- see
# tools/check-cc-symbols.py, which verifies every Cloudcell JNI symbol against
# the guest image and should be run after touching any Java_* literal.
.local/
# 20 throwaway probe scripts an agent left in tools/. Untracked 2026-10-19.
# They are all "_test_*" one-offs (chacha/decrypt/keys/sections/so_inspect/
# so_search, several numbered retries of the same idea). None is referenced by
# any tracked script or by Build-NativeSwitch.ps1 -- the real tooling lives in
# tools/guest-analysis/. Checked before ignoring, not after.
tools/_test_*.ps1

# --- run-time scratch written by the port -----------------------------------
crash_reports/
*.log
sdmc:/

# --- OS noise ---------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
desktop.ini
